WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.107 --> 00:00:05.413
- It’s-a me, Mario!

00:00:05.413 --> 00:00:07.213
It’s-a me, Mario!

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:08.880
Woo-hoo, let’s-a go!

00:00:09.773 --> 00:00:10.824
Okey dokey!

00:00:10.824 --> 00:00:12.443
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow!

00:00:12.443 --> 00:00:15.123
I've been the voice of Mario for 26 years.

00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:16.493
- [Interviewer] Now moving on to Luigi.

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:18.235
- Now moving on to Luigi, oh.

00:00:18.235 --> 00:00:19.068
(laughing)

00:00:19.068 --> 00:00:23.982
("Super Mario Overworld
Theme" by Koji Kondo)

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:25.125
Hi, I'm Charles Martinet.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:29.066
I do the voice of Super
Mario, here we go, woo hoo!

00:00:29.066 --> 00:00:32.244
And Luigi too, Luigi number one, ho ho!

00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:34.002
And Wario, have a rotten day.

00:00:34.002 --> 00:00:35.094
Yah-ho!

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:36.593
You gonna eat that garlic?

00:00:36.593 --> 00:00:38.133
(laughs)

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.937
and I was even Donkey Kong at one point.

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:41.291
Oh hoo hoo!

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.316
I am an actor and voice actor.

00:00:43.316 --> 00:00:46.267
I did gosh, 25 years of theatre.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.886
Run along to your party!

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:48.926
Corporate videos.

00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:51.785
Circuitry and semi-conductor processes.

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.546
A few film and television products.

00:00:53.546 --> 00:00:55.377
Now beat it all of ya, now!

00:00:55.377 --> 00:00:57.777
And then I had the marvelous beginning

00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:00.446
of becoming a voice actor
and that's how I started

00:01:00.446 --> 00:01:02.279
with it’s-a me, Mario!

00:01:04.032 --> 00:01:07.086
Mario was first created in 1981

00:01:07.086 --> 00:01:08.875
in a game called Donkey Kong.

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:10.545
As it got refined through the years,

00:01:10.545 --> 00:01:14.093
it became Mario and Princess Peach.

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:15.555
Ah, the Princess!

00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:17.795
And I came along in 1990.

00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:20.446
I actually crashed an audition
because I was catching

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.932
them as I walked in they
were walking out finished

00:01:22.932 --> 00:01:24.966
for the day and I said,
"can I read for this?"

00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:26.685
And the guy looked at
his watch and he goes,

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:27.957
"ugh, alright, come on in.

00:01:27.957 --> 00:01:29.917
"You're an Italian plumber from Brooklyn,

00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:32.251
"a character in a video game for Nintendo

00:01:32.251 --> 00:01:34.456
"called Mario so make up a voice,

00:01:34.456 --> 00:01:36.376
"make up a video game, start talking."

00:01:36.376 --> 00:01:38.325
And I thought to myself, video game?

00:01:38.325 --> 00:01:40.175
I don't know anything about video games

00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:41.523
and all of a sudden I hear action,

00:01:41.523 --> 00:01:44.135
I go "hello, I’m-a Mario, let's
make a pizza pie together.

00:01:44.135 --> 00:01:46.477
"You go get some-a sausage,
I’m-a go get some spaghetti,

00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:48.077
"we put spaghetti and-a
sausage in the pizza."

00:01:48.077 --> 00:01:50.957
And he said, "cut, stop
talking, there's no more tape,

00:01:50.957 --> 00:01:52.557
"alright thanks, we'll be in touch."

00:01:52.557 --> 00:01:53.945
And I thought that was, you know,

00:01:53.945 --> 00:01:55.349
okay there's the door, we'll see ya later.

00:01:55.349 --> 00:01:58.256
And he calls Nintendo, "I
found a Mario, I got him."

00:01:58.256 --> 00:02:01.923
And that was 26 amazing
fantastic years ago.

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:07.157
Hello!

00:02:07.157 --> 00:02:08.317
Hello!

00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:09.504
(laughs)

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:10.516
Whoo-pee!

00:02:10.516 --> 00:02:12.797
Oh, look at this world.

00:02:12.797 --> 00:02:15.665
The character for me
brings out the best in me

00:02:15.665 --> 00:02:17.087
and so I love that.

00:02:17.087 --> 00:02:19.133
Bing bing bing, (laughs)

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.339
I love sharing things too.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:21.917
I go to meet Mario fans

00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:23.987
and I hear the most wonderful things.

00:02:23.987 --> 00:02:26.128
You know, you're the voice of my childhood

00:02:26.128 --> 00:02:29.128
or I used to play with my dad,
now I'm playing with my kids.

00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:31.896
It's a way our family comes together.

00:02:31.896 --> 00:02:33.277
Ya ya ya ya ya, ha!

00:02:33.277 --> 00:02:34.610
Ah, pretty good!

00:02:35.946 --> 00:02:37.968
Ah, this brings back the memories.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:38.801
Mama mia!

00:02:39.756 --> 00:02:41.899
You just have fun, you know?

00:02:41.899 --> 00:02:43.397
That's my mantra for life.

00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:44.986
Come on, let’s-a go!

00:02:44.986 --> 00:02:46.419
Let's have more fun!

00:02:46.419 --> 00:02:48.447
Bye bye, see you in my gameses.

00:02:48.447 --> 00:02:49.280
Woo-hoo!

